&P355886 = JNES 14, 015 
#atf: lang sux 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. er-s,e2-tum-mi er-s,e2-tum 
#tr.ts: erṣetummi erṣetum 
#tr.en: The earth, they say, the earth 
2. u2-li-id lu-ha-ma 
#tr.ts: ūlid luḫammâ 
#tr.en: bore the mud; 
3. lu-hu-mu-u2 
#tr.ts: luhummû 
#tr.en: the mud  
4. u2-li-id2 i-szi-na 
#tr.ts: ūlid išīna 
#tr.en: bore the stalk; 
5. i-szi-nu-um u2-li-id 
#tr.ts: išīnum ūlid 
#tr.en: the stalk bore 
6. szu-bu-ul-tam{am} 
#tr.ts: šubultam 
#tr.en: the spike; 
7. szu-bu-ul-tum 
#tr.ts: šubultum 
#tr.en: the spike 
8. u2-li-id me-er-ha 
#tr.ts: ūlid merḫa 
#tr.en: bore the seed. 
9. i-na-mi _a-sza3_ {d}en-lil2 
#tr.ts: inami eqel ellil 
#tr.en: They say in the field of Enlil, 
10. mi-it-ha-ri-im 
#tr.ts: mitḫarim 
#tr.en: the square one, 
11. _sze asza5{a-sza3}_ 
#tr.ts: u’i eqlim 
#tr.en: the barley of the field 
12. {d}suen i-s,e2-di 
#tr.ts: sîn iṣṣedi 
#tr.en: Sin was harvesting, 
@reverse 
1. {d}utu u-sza-ap-ha-ar 
#tr.ts: šamaš ušapḫar 
#tr.en: Šamaš was gathering together. 
2. a-na-mi _igi gurusz_ 
#tr.ts: anami īn eṭlim 
#tr.en: They say into the eye of the man 
3. i-te-ru-ub
#tr.ts: īterub 
#tr.en: did enter 
4. me-er-hu-um 
#tr.ts: merḫum
#tr.en: the seed. 
5. ma-na lu-usz-pu-ur 
#tr.ts: manna lušpur 
#tr.en: Whom should I send 
6. u3 lu-wa-'i3-ir 
#tr.ts: u luwa’’ir 
#tr.en: and instruct 
7. a-na _dumu-munus_ an 7(disz@v) 7(disz@v) 
#tr.ts: ana marāt anim sebe sebe 
#tr.en: to the daughters of An, 7-7? 
8. li-il-qe2-nim
#tr.ts: lilqênim 
#tr.en: Let them take 
9. _{gesz#}gub_ sza sa-am-ti
#tr.ts: manzāzam ša samti 
#tr.en: a stand of carneol, 
10. _dug_ sza hu-la-lim 
#tr.ts: karpatam ša ḫulalim 
#tr.en: a pot of chalcedony; 
11. li-sa-ba-nim 
#tr.ts: lisābānim 
#tr.en: let them ladle out 
12. me tam!-tim 
#tr.ts: mê tâmtim 
#tr.en: water of the sea, 
13. el#-lu-tim me-er-ha 
#tr.ts: ellūtim merḫa 
#tr.en: pure, the seed 
14. li#-sze#-li-[a] 
#tr.ts: lišēli'ā 
#tr.en: let them lift out 
15. [i]-na _igi gurusz_
#tr.ts: ina īn eṭlim 
#tr.en: from the eye of the man.

